{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TZrP9mVGhripr1La5sYSE5","type":"tool_result","content":"```\n\nSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n\n## Getting started\n\nPick credentials: a GitHub App (see Getting started), a personal access token in `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` (a fine-grained, single-repo token with an expiry is best), or nothing, in which case `ard serve` uses a logged-in `gh` CLI's token for the session. `ard serve` checks the credentials against the repository before it starts any loop. Then install the App if you use one, run `ard init`, commit and merge the tree, run `ard setup`, fix any manual rows it reports, try `ard serve --dry-run`, then go live. See [Getting started](docs/site/getting-started.md).\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Go (see `go.mod`).\n\n```bash\nmake build   # builds bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet and a gofmt check\n```\n\nContributor and agent guidance is in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n\n## License\n\n[GPL-3.0](LICENSE)\n- **Agents write only their own files.** Close-out lets a job change under `.ard/<issue#>/` only its own role file and what its role owns (a `plan.md` section, `design/`); anything else fails the job \n- **Role files are human-owned.** The diff guard and the committer's code lane reject any worker change under `.ard/` or `.github/` (so `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ard/PRODUCT.md`, `.ard/VISION.md`, `.ard/T\n- **The tag-writing credential is separate.** Only the `tag` job of `version.yml`, in the `release` environment, holds a token that can push tags, from a release App that must differ from ard's App (t\n- **Merges are gated.** The merger lands a PR only when every review passed and required checks (read from the branch rules API) are green on an up-to-date branch; protected paths wait for a write-acc\n- **Agent text cannot close issues.** Agent text in a commit message, PR title or PR body has closing references neutralised (`committer.NeutraliseRefs`: \"Fixes #12\" becomes \"Fixes issue 12\"). Only a \nconfiguration.md\ngetting-started.md\nindex.md\ninstall.md\noperations\noperations.md\nrequirements.txt\nroles\nsecurity.md\ntroubleshooting.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"1561fa7a-e7f3-45b1-b505-c43316cd1390","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:04.314Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"```\n\nSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n\n## Getting started\n\nPick credentials: a GitHub App (see Getting started), a personal access token in `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` (a fine-grained, single-repo token with an expiry is best), or nothing, in which case `ard serve` uses a logged-in `gh` CLI's token for the session. `ard serve` checks the credentials against the repository before it starts any loop. Then install the App if you use one, run `ard init`, commit and merge the tree, run `ard setup`, fix any manual rows it reports, try `ard serve --dry-run`, then go live. See [Getting started](docs/site/getting-started.md).\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Go (see `go.mod`).\n\n```bash\nmake build   # builds bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet and a gofmt check\n```\n\nContributor and agent guidance is in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n\n## License\n\n[GPL-3.0](LICENSE)\n- **Agents write only their own files.** Close-out lets a job change under `.ard/<issue#>/` only its own role file and what its role owns (a `plan.md` section, `design/`); anything else fails the job \n- **Role files are human-owned.** The diff guard and the committer's code lane reject any worker change under `.ard/` or `.github/` (so `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ard/PRODUCT.md`, `.ard/VISION.md`, `.ard/T\n- **The tag-writing credential is separate.** Only the `tag` job of `version.yml`, in the `release` environment, holds a token that can push tags, from a release App that must 