{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChS4aL2ugPyDTQ36RkVE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HtB99Dd6MJ24YCRCVxAbGd","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/work/README.md","old_string":"## Development\n\nRequires","new_string":"## Install\n\nWith Homebrew (macOS and Linux):\n\n```bash\nbrew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard\nard version\n```\n\nUpgrade with `brew upgrade --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard` (or plain `brew upgrade`). `brew uninstall --cask ard` removes the binary only; it leaves `~/.ard/` (state, locks, pause files) alone, so delete that directory by hand if you want it gone.\n\nThe cask depends on the `git` formula. You still need the `claude` CLI and a model credential (`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` or an API key) in the environment.\n\nThe binary is not yet signed or notarized, so the cask clears the macOS quarantine flag after install (`hooks.post.install` in the cask). This is an accepted risk; see [Guardrails](docs/proposal.md#guardrails). Notarization is the follow-up.\n\nBuilding from source still works; see Development below and [Install](docs/site/install.md).\n\n## Development\n\nRequires"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1004,"cache_read_input_tokens":25337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1004},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"383a1829-51ff-4772-b507-a09ba64f1ab3","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:07.697Z","request_id":"req_011ChS4aKsjrNW1R8SKW6WWx"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HtB99Dd6MJ24YCRCVxAbGd","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /work/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"71ebf9ed-1977-45dd-96a0-9d963a827f7b","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:07.759Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/work/README.md","oldString":"## Development\n\nRequires","newString":"## Install\n\nWith Homebrew (macOS and Linux):\n\n```bash\nbrew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard\nard version\n```\n\nUpgrade with `brew upgrade --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard` (or plain `brew upgrade`). `brew uninstall --cask ard` removes the binary only; it leaves `~/.ard/` (state, locks, pause files) alone, so delete that directory by hand if you want it gone.\n\nThe cask depends on the `git` formula. You still need the `claude` CLI and a model credential (`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` or an API key) in the environment.\n\nThe binary is not yet signed or notarized, so the cask clears the macOS quarantine flag after install (`hooks.post.install` in the cask). This is an accepted risk; see [Guardrails](docs/proposal.md#guardrails). Notarization is the follow-up.\n\nBuilding from source still works; see Development below and [Install](docs/site/install.md).\n\n## Development\n\nRequires","originalFile":"# ard — automated repository development\n\nard makes a GitHub repository maintain itself. Scanners file deduplicated issues, triage agents turn each issue into a plan, a worker agent implements it on a branch, reviewer agents critique the PR, and a merger lands it once every review passes.\n\n**Documentation:** <https://albertcbrown.github.io/ard/> (sources in [docs/site](docs/site)).\n\n> **Status:** under active development. The design lives in [docs/proposal.md](docs/proposal.md), and the work is tracked as [GitHub issues](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues) grouped into phase milestones.\n\n## How it works\n\nOne rule holds the system together: **a deterministic controller owns every GitHub and git side effect; agents only read and write files in a worktree.**\n\nOne `ard` process per repository runs six loops that share a small pool of job slots (default 3):\n\n| Loop | Every | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Scanners | 4 h | Find problems (CVEs, outdated components, lint, docs, missing tests…), file or update issues, close what is fixed |\n| Triage | 15 min | Role agents (lead, PM, architect, designer, doc planner, engineer) turn an issue into `plan.md` |\n| Workers | 5 min | Implement the plan on `worker/<role>-<issue#>-<slug>`, run tests, open a draft PR |\n| Reviewers | 5 min | Role agents (security, license, eng, PM) review the PR and request fixes |\n| Merger | 5 min | Squash-merge PRs whose reviews all passed and whose checks are green |\n| Reaper | 1 min | Mark dead or overdue jobs `ard:executor:failed`, keep their evidence 24 h |\n\nGitHub labels prefixed `ard:` are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` in the target repository holds each issue's plan, per-role summaries and full agent logs.\n\n## Configuration by convention\n\nA target repository opts in with an `.ard/` directory. A role exists because its directory exists:\n\n```\n.ard/\n├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\n├── scanners/<name>/     # scan (executable) or prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── triage/<name>/       # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── workers/<name>/      # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n└── <issue#>/            # per-issue output and logs, written only by ard\n```\n\nSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n\n## Getting started\n\nPick credentials: a GitHub App (see Getting started), a personal access token in `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` (a fine-grained, single-repo token with an expiry is best), or nothing, in which case `ard serve` uses a logged-in `gh` CLI's token for the session. `ard serve` checks the credentials against the repository before it starts any loop. Then install the App if you use one, run `ard init`, commit and merge the tree, run `ard setup`, fix any manual rows it reports, try `ard serve --dry-run`, then go live. See [Getting started](docs/site/getting-started.md).\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Go (see `go.mod`).\n\n```bash\nmake build   # builds bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet and a gofmt check\n```\n\nContributor and agent guidance is in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n\n## License\n\n[GPL-3.0](LICENSE)\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":43,"oldLines":6,"newStart":43,"newLines":23,"lines":[" "," Pick credentials: a GitHub App (see Getting started), a personal access token in `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` (a fine-grained, single-repo token with an expiry is best), or nothing, in which case `ard serve` uses a logged-in `gh` CLI's token for the session. `ard serve` checks the credentials against the repository before it starts any loop. Then install the App if you use one, run `ard init`, commit and merge the tree, run `ard setup`, fix any manual rows it reports, try `ard serve --dry-run`, then go live. See [Getting started](docs/site/getting-started.md)."," ","+## Install","+","+With Homebrew (macOS and Linux):","+","+```bash","+brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard","+ard version","+```","+","+Upgrade with `brew upgrade --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard` (or plain `brew upgrade`). `brew uninstall --cask ard` removes the binary only; it leaves `~/.ard/` (state, locks, pause files) alone, so delete that directory by hand if you want it gone.","+","+The cask depends on the `git` formula. You still need the `claude` CLI and a model credential (`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` or an API key) in the environment.","+","+The binary is not yet signed or notarized, so the cask clears the macOS quarantine flag after install (`hooks.post.install` in the cask). This is an accepted risk; see [Guardrails](docs/proposal.md#guardrails). Notarization is the follow-up.","+","+Building from source still works; see Development below and [Install](docs/site/install.md).","+"," ## Development"," "," Requires Go (see `go.mod`)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HtB99Dd6MJ24YCRCVxAbGd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
