{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LrW7w2pBaHjWkSMC46C27B","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /work/docs/site/install.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"6492bc34-2f86-41d4-8e67-7f21056be550","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:09.902Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/work/docs/site/install.md","oldString":" A Homebrew cask is planned (#177); this page will point to it once it lands.","newString":"","originalFile":"# Install\n\nard runs on macOS and Linux. It needs:\n\n- Go (to build), `make` and `git` 2.47.0 or newer. An older git fails some fetches.\n- The `claude` CLI for the default agent.\n- Docker, only for roles that ship a `Dockerfile` (the cve, docs and lint scanners).\n\n## Homebrew\n\n```sh\nbrew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard\nard version\n```\n\nUpgrade with `brew upgrade --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`. `brew uninstall --cask ard` removes the binary and leaves `~/.ard/` alone. The binary is not yet signed or notarized, so the cask clears the macOS quarantine flag after install (`hooks.post.install`); see the Guardrails section of the proposal.\n\n## Build from source\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard\ncd ard\nmake build\n./bin/ard version\n```\n\nPut `bin/ard` on your `PATH`. A Homebrew cask is planned (#177); this page will point to it once it lands.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":4,"newStart":24,"newLines":4,"lines":[" ./bin/ard version"," ```"," ","-Put `bin/ard` on your `PATH`. A Homebrew cask is planned (#177); this page will point to it once it lands.","+Put `bin/ard` on your `PATH`.","\\ No newline at end of file"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LrW7w2pBaHjWkSMC46C27B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChS4aL2ugPyDTQ36RkVE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LXgy6XXqZUMZu4PpqgHxbZ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/work/docs/runbooks/release.md","old_string":"This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n","new_string":"This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## How a merge becomes a release\n\n1. A merge to `main` makes `version.yml` push the next `vX.Y.Z` tag and create a notes-only release for it.\n2. The `v*` tag push starts `release.yml`. GoReleaser builds four archives and `checksums.txt` and uploads them to that existing release (`release.mode: keep-existing`).\n3. GoReleaser then commits `Casks/ard.rb` to `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`, using `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`.\n4. Check it: `brew update && brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`, then `ard version`.\n\nThe one-time setup (release App, variables, `release` environment, tag ruleset, tap and token) is below; nothing publishes until it is done and `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`.\n\n**One release at a time.** `release.yml` uses `concurrency: release` with `cancel-in-progress: false`, so a second run queues behind the first and never cancels an upload in progress.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1004,"cache_read_input_tokens":25337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1004},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"12f80057-20e3-47b0-8c31-e00010a703c0","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:12.696Z","request_id":"req_011ChS4aKsjrNW1R8SKW6WWx"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LXgy6XXqZUMZu4PpqgHxbZ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /work/docs/runbooks/release.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"1eca7431-048e-40b0-a914-4530a7218537","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:12.706Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/work/docs/runbooks/release.md","oldString":"This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n","newString":"This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## How a merge becomes a release\n\n1. A merge to `main` makes `version.yml` push the next `vX.Y.Z` tag and create a notes-only release for it.\n2. The `v*` tag push starts `release.yml`. GoReleaser builds four archives and `checksums.txt` and uploads them to that existing release (`release.mode: keep-existing`).\n3. GoReleaser then commits `Casks/ard.rb` to `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`, using `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`.\n4. Check it: `brew update && brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`, then `ard version`.\n\nThe one-time setup (release App, variables, `release` environment, tag ruleset, tap and token) is below; nothing publishes until it is done and `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`.\n\n**One release at a time.** `release.yml` uses `concurrency: release` with `cancel-in-progress: false`, so a second run queues behind the first and never cancels an upload in progress.\n","originalFile":"# Release runbook\n\n`.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## Seed tag\n\nAn admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:\n\n```\ngit tag -a v0.1.0 <sha> -m v0.1.0\ngit push origin refs/tags/v0.1.0\n```\n\nUntil it exists a dry run plans nothing and a live run fails.\n\n## Settings checklist\n\n- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n- A `release` environment holding the secret `RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. The release App needs contents: write only, and must not be ard's App.\n- A tag ruleset on `v*` that only the release App may bypass.\n- For Homebrew: the secret `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN` in the same `release` environment, and the `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` repository (see Homebrew release).\n\nThe steps below set these up once. They use `ard-release` as the App's name; use any name that is free, and substitute it throughout.\n\n## Create the release App\n\n`version.yml`'s `tag` job mints a short-lived token from this App (`actions/create-github-app-token`) to push tags and create releases. It is a separate App from ard's so that ard's own token can never create a tag; the job refuses to run if the two are the same (it compares the App's slug with `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`).\n\n1. Open <https://github.com/settings/apps/new> (for an organization: the organization's Settings → Developer settings → GitHub Apps → New GitHub App).\n   - **GitHub App name:** `ard-release`. **Homepage URL:** the repository URL.\n   - **Webhook:** clear **Active**. The App receives no events.\n   - **Repository permissions:** **Contents: Read and write**. Leave every other permission at **No access** (Metadata stays read-only, as GitHub requires).\n   - **Where can this GitHub App be installed?** **Only on this account**.\n   - Select **Create GitHub App**.\n2. On the App's page, note the **App ID**. Under **Private keys**, select **Generate a private key**; the browser downloads a `.pem` file.\n3. Select **Install App**, choose the account, then **Only select repositories** → `albertcbrown/ard`. Install it on nothing else.\n4. Set the repository variables. The tagger email is the bot's noreply address, which needs the bot account's numeric user ID:\n\n   ```\n   gh api '/users/ard-release[bot]' -q .id\n   gh variable set RELEASE_APP_ID    -R albertcbrown/ard -b '<app-id>'\n   gh variable set RELEASE_BOT_NAME  -R albertcbrown/ard -b 'ard-release[bot]'\n   gh variable set RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL -R albertcbrown/ard -b '<bot-user-id>+ard-release[bot]@users.noreply.github.com'\n   ```\n\n   Check that `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` is also set to ard's own App login (`gh variable list -R albertcbrown/ard`).\n5. Create the `release` environment and store the key only there, then delete the downloaded file:\n\n   ```\n   gh api -X PUT repos/albertcbrown/ard/environments/release\n   gh secret set RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY -R albertcbrown/ard --env release < ~/Downloads/ard-release.<date>.private-key.pem\n   rm ~/Downloads/ard-release.<date>.private-key.pem\n   ```\n\n   Optionally restrict the environment's deployment branches and tags to `main` and `v*` (Settings → Environments → release), so only runs from those refs can read its secrets.\n\nTo rotate the key, generate a new one on the App page, run the `gh secret set` line again with it, then delete the old key on the App page.\n\n## Protect the tags\n\nA tag ruleset keeps tags immutable and lets only the release App create them. `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`'s App, workflows using `GITHUB_TOKEN` and people without bypass cannot create, move or delete a `v*` tag.\n\n```\ngh api -X POST repos/albertcbrown/ard/rulesets --input - <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"name\": \"release tags\",\n  \"target\": \"tag\",\n  \"enforcement\": \"active\",\n  \"conditions\": { \"ref_name\": { \"include\": [\"refs/tags/v*\"], \"exclude\": [] } },\n  \"rules\": [ { \"type\": \"creation\" }, { \"type\": \"update\" }, { \"type\": \"deletion\" } ],\n  \"bypass_actors\": [ { \"actor_id\": <app-id>, \"actor_type\": \"Integration\", \"bypass_mode\": \"always\" } ]\n}\nEOF\n```\n\n`actor_id` is the release App's **App ID** (the same number as `RELEASE_APP_ID`). The same ruleset can be made in Settings → Rules → Rulesets → New tag ruleset: target `v*`, enable **Restrict creations**, **Restrict updates** and **Restrict deletions**, and add the App under **Bypass list**. Check it with `gh api repos/albertcbrown/ard/rulesets`.\n\nThe seed tag (above) must exist before the ruleset, or an admin must be added to the bypass list while creating it and removed afterwards.\n\n## Turn it on\n\n1. Run a dry run and read the plan in the run's step summary:\n\n   ```\n   gh workflow run version.yml -R albertcbrown/ard\n   gh run watch -R albertcbrown/ard \"$(gh run list -R albertcbrown/ard -w version.yml -L 1 --json databaseId -q '.[0].databaseId')\"\n   ```\n\n2. Set `ARD_VERSIONING` to `on` (`gh variable set ARD_VERSIONING -R albertcbrown/ard -b on`).\n3. Run live, raising `max_tags` when the dry run planned more than 20 tags:\n\n   ```\n   gh workflow run version.yml -R albertcbrown/ard -f dry_run=false -f max_tags=60\n   ```\n\n   A failure that names a variable or the App points at the step above that sets it; fix it and rerun (see Recovery).\n\n## Homebrew release (release.yml)\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml` runs on each `v*` tag `version.yml` pushes (and on `workflow_dispatch` with a `tag`). It builds the four archives with GoReleaser (`.goreleaser.yaml`), uploads them and `checksums.txt` to the tag's existing release, and updates `Casks/ard.rb` in `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`.\n\n- It does nothing until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on` **and** the `release` environment holds the secret `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`. Without the token it logs a notice and stops.\n- `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`: a fine-grained token (or a second App's token) with **contents: read and write on `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` only**. Store it only in the `release` environment.\n- Create `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` (public, with a `Casks/` directory) and protect its `main`.\n\nTo set up the tap and its token:\n\n1. Create the tap repository with a `Casks/` directory:\n\n   ```\n   gh repo create albertcbrown/homebrew-tap --public --description \"Homebrew tap for ard\"\n   gh repo clone albertcbrown/homebrew-tap && cd homebrew-tap\n   mkdir Casks && touch Casks/.gitkeep && git add Casks && git commit -m \"Add Casks directory\" && git push origin HEAD:main\n   ```\n\n2. Create the token at <https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new>: **Resource owner** `albertcbrown`, **Repository access** → **Only select repositories** → `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`, **Repository permissions** → **Contents: Read and write**, nothing else. Pick an expiry and note it; the release stops with a push error when it lapses.\n3. Store it in the `release` environment only. `gh` prompts for the value, so it stays out of shell history:\n\n   ```\n   gh secret set TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN -R albertcbrown/ard --env release\n   ```\n\n4. Protect the tap's `main` (Settings → Rules → New branch ruleset: block force pushes and deletions). GoReleaser commits `Casks/ard.rb` directly, so do not require pull requests there.\n5. Rotate the token before it expires: create a new one and run step 3 again, then revoke the old one.\n- On a tag push only the newest `v*` tag is released, so a backfill of many tags publishes once. To build an older tag: `gh workflow run release.yml -R albertcbrown/ard -f tag=vX.Y.Z`.\n- One release runs at a time (`concurrency: release`, never cancelled).\n- Check locally first: `make release-check` (snapshot, publishes nothing).\n\n## Dry run to live\n\nEvery run is a dry run until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. Check the plan in a dry run's step summary, then set the variable. `workflow_dispatch` is a dry run unless `dry_run` is false; `max_tags` (default 20) caps the tags one run creates, so raise it after reading the plan when a backlog is larger.\n\n## Bumps and the module path\n\nLabel a PR `semver:minor` or `semver:major`; with neither it is a patch, and with both major wins. Go requires a `/vN` module path for N >= 2. A `semver:major` that would reach v2 stops the run (exit 2) until `go.mod` says `module .../v2`; relabel the PR or change `go.mod`, then rerun.\n\n## Recovery\n\n- A failed run stops at the first failure. Rerun it: the plan is rebuilt from the tags that exist, and a tag without a release gets a release-only backfill row.\n- Never delete or move a tag. If a tag is wrong, fix forward with the next version.\n- `ard version` prints the tag after `make build` on a tagged commit, and after `go install github.com/albertcbrown/ard/cmd/ard@vX.Y.Z`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":17,"lines":[" "," `.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow."," ","+## How a merge becomes a release","+","+1. A merge to `main` makes `version.yml` push the next `vX.Y.Z` tag and create a notes-only release for it.","+2. The `v*` tag push starts `release.yml`. GoReleaser builds four archives and `checksums.txt` and uploads them to that existing release (`release.mode: keep-existing`).","+3. GoReleaser then commits `Casks/ard.rb` to `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`, using `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`.","+4. Check it: `brew update && brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`, then `ard version`.","+","+The one-time setup (release App, variables, `release` environment, tag ruleset, tap and token) is below; nothing publishes until it is done and `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`.","+","+**One release at a time.** `release.yml` uses `concurrency: release` with `cancel-in-progress: false`, so a second run queues behind the first and never cancels an upload in progress.","+"," ## Seed tag"," "," An admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LXgy6XXqZUMZu4PpqgHxbZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChS4aL2ugPyDTQ36RkVE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01182eiwwAtfb4xvGz14PGug","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/runbooks/release.md <<'EOF'\n\n### A failed release.yml run\n\n`goreleaser release --clean` rebuilds everything from the tag, and with `release.mode: keep-existing` it adds files to the existing release instead of replacing its notes, so rerunning is the normal fix.\n\n- Read the failed step. \"no release for vX.Y.Z\" means `version.yml` has not created the release yet; rerun `version.yml` first.\n- Rerun the failed run (`gh run rerun <run-id> -R albertcbrown/ard --failed`). If a newer tag has since been pushed, a rerun of an older tag's push run skips (\"not the newest tag\"); use `gh workflow run release.yml -R albertcbrown/ard -f tag=vX.Y.Z` instead.\n- A push error on the tap means `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN` has expired or lacks contents: write on `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`. Replace it (see Homebrew release), then rerun.\n- If the assets uploaded but the cask did not update, rerun the same way; the cask is regenerated from the tag.\n- A bad release is never fixed by moving its tag. Fix forward with the next version.\n\n### Gatekeeper\n\nThe binary is not signed or notarized. The cask clears the quarantine flag after install, in its `hooks.post.install` stanza (an `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine` on the installed `ard`), so macOS does not block the first run. This is an accepted risk, recorded in the Guardrails section of `docs/proposal.md`. Notarization is the follow-up; when it lands, drop the hook from `.goreleaser.yaml`.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\nL=open(p).read().split('\\n')\ni=next(k for k,l in enumerate(L) if l.startswith('- **The tag-writing credential is separate.**'))\nL.insert(i+1,\"- **Gatekeeper: unsigned binary, quarantine cleared (accepted risk).** The release binary is neither signed nor notarized. The Homebrew cask removes `com.apple.quarantine` from the installed binary in `hooks.post.install`, which skips Gatekeeper's check, so the install path trusts the release archive, its checksum and whoever holds `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`. The owner accepts this. The follow-up is Developer ID signing and notarization in the release workflow, after which the hook is removed.\")\ns='\\n'.join(L)\ns=s.replace(\"a Homebrew cask (`brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`).\",\"a Homebrew cask (`brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`). It ships the README Install section and the release runbook (`docs/runbooks/release.md`).\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; make lint test 2>&1 | tail -5; git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1004,"cache_read_input_tokens":25337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1004},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7eb1afcb-ed8c-476d-bb5f-6257ca4c1350","uuid":"feca3193-2ba4-4d30-98d2-7d74db7a2ecf","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:06:18.967Z","request_id":"req_011ChS4aKsjrNW1R8SKW6WWx"}
